1.2 Sociodemographic characteristics
nationality
The results show that out of the 7 , 092,1 13 persons who spent Census night in Sierra Leone, 99.4 percent are
Sierra Leoneans and 0.6 percent are non-Sierra Leoneans.
Marital Status
The 2015 PHC results reveal that 30 percent of the population 10 years and above at the national are in
polygamous marriage, 13 percent in monogamous marriage and 45.9 percent never married. The male
population 10 years and above is more likely to be never married (53.1%) than their female counterparts
(39.1%). The female population is almost 8 times more likely to be widowed (7 .0%) than the male population
(0.9%).
Fertility
The total fertility rate (TFR) is estimated at 5.2 children per woman, compared to 6.1 in 2004. At the regional
level, the TFR is estimated at 5.4 children per woman in the Eastern region, 5.6 in the Northern region, 5.5 in
the Southern region and 4.0 in the Western Area.
